    "https://thei.edu.hk/professor-associate-professor-ref-o-thei-ddit-professorialddit-11-25/": {
      "title": "Professor / Associate Professor",
      "description": "Professor / Associate Professor - Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong Back About Vision and Mission Senior Management Strategic Plan Governance & Organisation Departments Department of Construction, Environment and Engineering Department of Design and Architecture Department of Digital Innovation and Technology Department of Food and Health Sciences Department of Hospitality and Business Management Department of Sport and Recreation School of General Education and Languages Current Student Admission Research THEi Research Centre Applied Impact Research Students Applied Research Presentations Research Repository Collaboration Work-Study Degree Programmes Work-Study Degree Scheme for BSE On-the-job-training Allowance Pilot Scheme Work-integrated Learning THEi – Lions Clubs Innov8 Enterprise Start-up Centre Employ our students News & Media Rooms Visitors Getting To THEi Visiting THEi Local School or Academic Organisation General Public or Other Organisations Facilities THEi Souvenirs Dining Society Smoke-Free Campus Contact Us Publication Staff Jobs EN 繁 简 Staff Jobs EN 繁 简 About Vision and Mission Senior Management Strategic Plan Governance & Organisation Departments Department of Construction, Environment and Engineering Department of Design and Architecture Department of Digital Innovation and Technology Department of Food and Health Sciences Department of Hospitality and Business Management Department of Sport and Recreation School of General Education and Languages Current Student Admission Research THEi Research Centre Applied Impact Research Students Applied Research Presentations Research Repository Collaboration Work-Study Degree Programmes Work-Study Degree Scheme for BSE On-the-job-training Allowance Pilot Scheme Work-integrated Learning THEi – Lions Clubs Innov8 Enterprise Start-up Centre Employ our students News & Media Rooms Visitors Getting To THEi Visiting THEi Local School or Academic Organisation General Public or Other Organisations Facilities THEi Souvenirs Dining Society Smoke-Free Campus Contact Us Publication ✕ Post Specification TITLE : Professor / Associate Professor Department of Digital Innovation and Technology Ref No.: DDIT/PROFESSORIAL(DDIT)/11/25 Major Duties: The appointee is expected to provide strong academic leadership by contributing to the planning, development, implementation and review of the academic programmes under the Department of Digital Innovation and Technology.  The appointee will also provide strong academic leadership in the formulation of learning and teaching strategies; curriculum development of programme modules for the academic programmes in the Department; and research activities in the field of Computer Science & Information Technology, particularly in Artificial Intelligence, Cyber Security, Human-Computer Interaction, Computer Graphics, Multimedia Technology and Game Technology. The appointee will take part in teaching and supervising student work; delivering quality programmes; and leading and participating in scholarly activities, including but not limited to research, consultancy, networking, collaboration with industry and promoting the Institute and the programmes.  The appointee will also be expected to maintain close contacts with industry, commerce, and other educational institutes on collaborative arrangements to promote and ensure the relevance and excellence of the programmes. Requirements: The successful candidate should have a recognised Doctoral degree in Computer Science, Information Science, Artificial Intelligence, Human-Computer Interaction, Computer Graphics, or a related area, with relevant teaching experience at tertiary level; demonstrated achievement in research and scholarly activities, and experience in professional practice in the relevant fields.  The candidate should have good interpersonal and communication skills, and possess high proficiency in written and spoken English and Chinese, including Putonghua.  Proven record of linkage with industry or professional bodies would be an advantage. Notes: (1) The appointee may be required to perform duties at different location, including outside Hong Kong, and work irregular hours, shifts, and on weekends as necessary. (2) The remuneration package will be competitive and commensurate with the appointee’s qualifications and experience. (3) The appointee will work at the Chai Wan Campus. Application Procedures: A completed application form [THEi-HR-601 (Dec 2025)] , together with a f ull curriculum vitae , should be sent to thei-jobs@thei.edu.hk . Applicants should take note of the following: (1) Completed application form and detailed curriculum vitae (CV) should be combined into one PDF file with a file size below 10MB . (2) The file should be saved with the applicant’s name as “surname and given name”, e.g. “CHAN Siu-lam.pdf”. (3) For the email subject, please cite “Application for Professor / Associate Professor (DDIT) (Ref No.: DDIT/PROFESSORIAL(DDIT)/11/25)”. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until the post is filled. The Institute reserves the right not to fill the post. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. Information on unsuccessful candidates will normally be destroyed 12 months after the completion of the recruitment exercise. Download Application Form in PDF format 3890 8000 3890 8339 info@thei.edu.hk 133 Shing Tai Road,  Chai Wan, Hong Kong Rm C215a, 2/F, Blk C, IVE(TY), 20 Tsing Yi Rd, Tsing Yi Island, NT Connect with THEi Resources For Current Students For Staff For Alumni For Visitors Copyright © 2026. Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong. All rights reserved. Privacy Disclaimer 3890 8000 3890 8339 info@thei.edu.hk 133 Shing Tai Road,  Chai Wan, Hong Kong Rm C215a, 2/F, Blk C, IVE(TY), 20 Tsing Yi Rd, Tsing Yi Island, NT Connect with THEi Resources For Current Students For Staff For Alumni For Visitors Copyright © 2026. Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong. All rights reserved. Privacy Disclaimer Login with your site account Lost your password? Remember Me"
    },
    "https://thei.edu.hk/professor-associate-professor-ref-no-dsr-professorial-05-26/": {
      "title": "Professor / Associate Professor",
      "description": "Professor / Associate Professor - Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong Back About Vision and Mission Senior Management Strategic Plan Governance & Organisation Departments Department of Construction, Environment and Engineering Department of Design and Architecture Department of Digital Innovation and Technology Department of Food and Health Sciences Department of Hospitality and Business Management Department of Sport and Recreation School of General Education and Languages Current Student Admission Research THEi Research Centre Applied Impact Research Students Applied Research Presentations Research Repository Collaboration Work-Study Degree Programmes Work-Study Degree Scheme for BSE On-the-job-training Allowance Pilot Scheme Work-integrated Learning THEi – Lions Clubs Innov8 Enterprise Start-up Centre Employ our students News & Media Rooms Visitors Getting To THEi Visiting THEi Local School or Academic Organisation General Public or Other Organisations Facilities THEi Souvenirs Dining Society Smoke-Free Campus Contact Us Publication Staff Jobs EN 繁 简 Staff Jobs EN 繁 简 About Vision and Mission Senior Management Strategic Plan Governance & Organisation Departments Department of Construction, Environment and Engineering Department of Design and Architecture Department of Digital Innovation and Technology Department of Food and Health Sciences Department of Hospitality and Business Management Department of Sport and Recreation School of General Education and Languages Current Student Admission Research THEi Research Centre Applied Impact Research Students Applied Research Presentations Research Repository Collaboration Work-Study Degree Programmes Work-Study Degree Scheme for BSE On-the-job-training Allowance Pilot Scheme Work-integrated Learning THEi – Lions Clubs Innov8 Enterprise Start-up Centre Employ our students News & Media Rooms Visitors Getting To THEi Visiting THEi Local School or Academic Organisation General Public or Other Organisations Facilities THEi Souvenirs Dining Society Smoke-Free Campus Contact Us Publication ✕ Post Specification TITLE : Professor / Associate Professor Department of Sport and Recreation Ref No.: DSR/PROFESSORIAL/05/26 Major Duties : The appointee is expected to provide strong academic leadership by contributing to the planning, development, implementation, and review of the academic programmes under the Department of Sport and Recreation.  The appointee will oversee the Bachelor of Social Sciences (Honours) in Sports Therapy programme and/or related programme(s) under the Department.  The appointee will also provide strong academic and management leadership in the formulation of learning and teaching strategies, cross-disciplinary curriculum development of programme modules for the academic programmes in the Department, student recruitment, and programme accreditation exercises. The appointee will take part in teaching and supervising honours projects and student work; delivering high-quality programmes; and leading and participating in scholarly activities, including but not limited to research, consultancy, networking, collaboration with industry, and promoting the Institute and the programmes.  The appointee will also be expected to maintain close contacts with industry, commerce, and other educational institutions on collaborative arrangements to promote and ensure the relevance and excellence of the programmes. Requirements : The successful candidate should have a recognised Doctoral degree in Physiotherapy, Sports Physiotherapy, Sports Therapy, or a related area, with relevant and substantial teaching experience at tertiary level; demonstrated excellent academic and management leadership; strong sports-related industry networks and work experience; a record of achievement in cross-disciplinary research and scholarly activities; and experience in accreditation exercises.  The candidate should have good interpersonal, communication, and problem-solving skills, and a high level of proficiency in written and spoken English and Chinese, including Putonghua.  A proven record of linkage with industry or professional bodies would be an advantage.  Experience in arranging student internships, supervising honours projects, managing funded projects, and the use of technological devices for teaching and research would also be an advantage. The appointee should be a registered physiotherapist or sports therapist, or have good potential for registration with the Physiotherapists Board of Hong Kong, or the Society of Sports Therapists (UK), or equivalent. Notes : (1) The appointee may be required to perform duties at different locations and outside Hong Kong, and to work irregular hours, shifts and weekends, as necessary. (2) The remuneration package will be competitive and commensurate with the appointee’s qualifications and experience. (3) The appointee will work at the Chai Wan Campus and/or nearby teaching premises. Application Procedures : A completed application form [THEi-HR-601 (Dec 2025)] , together with a f ull curriculum vitae (CV) , should be sent to thei-jobs@thei.edu.hk . Applicants should take note of the following: (1) The completed application form and detailed CV should be combined into one PDF file with a file size below 10MB . (2) The file should be saved with the applicant’s name as “surname and given name”, e.g. “CHAN Siu-lam.pdf”. (3) For the email subject, please cite “Application for Professor / Associate Professor (Ref No.: DSR/PROFESSORIAL/05/26)”. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until the post is filled. The Institute reserves the right not to fill the post.  Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only.  Information on unsuccessful candidates will normally be destroyed 12 months after completion of the recruitment exercise. Download Application Form in PDF format 3890 8000 3890 8339 info@thei.edu.hk 133 Shing Tai Road,  Chai Wan, Hong Kong Rm C215a, 2/F, Blk C, IVE(TY), 20 Tsing Yi Rd, Tsing Yi Island, NT Connect with THEi Resources For Current Students For Staff For Alumni For Visitors Copyright © 2026. Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong. All rights reserved. Privacy Disclaimer 3890 8000 3890 8339 info@thei.edu.hk 133 Shing Tai Road,  Chai Wan, Hong Kong Rm C215a, 2/F, Blk C, IVE(TY), 20 Tsing Yi Rd, Tsing Yi Island, NT Connect with THEi Resources For Current Students For Staff For Alumni For Visitors Copyright © 2026. Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong. All rights reserved. Privacy Disclaimer Login with your site account Lost your password? Remember Me"
    },
    "https://thei.edu.hk/professor-associate-professor-assistant-professor-master-of-science-in-urban-forestry-ref-no-dcee-professorial-mscuf-09-26/": {
      "title": "Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (Master of Science in Urban Forestry)",
      "description": "Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (Master of Science in Urban Forestry) - Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong Back About Vision and Mission Senior Management Strategic Plan Governance & Organisation Departments Department of Construction, Environment and Engineering Department of Design and Architecture Department of Digital Innovation and Technology Department of Food and Health Sciences Department of Hospitality and Business Management Department of Sport and Recreation School of General Education and Languages Current Student Admission Research THEi Research Centre Applied Impact Research Students Applied Research Presentations Research Repository Collaboration Work-Study Degree Programmes Work-Study Degree Scheme for BSE On-the-job-training Allowance Pilot Scheme Work-integrated Learning THEi – Lions Clubs Innov8 Enterprise Start-up Centre Employ our students News & Media Rooms Visitors Getting To THEi Visiting THEi Local School or Academic Organisation General Public or Other Organisations Facilities THEi Souvenirs Dining Society Smoke-Free Campus Contact Us Publication Staff Jobs EN 繁 简 Staff Jobs EN 繁 简 About Vision and Mission Senior Management Strategic Plan Governance & Organisation Departments Department of Construction, Environment and Engineering Department of Design and Architecture Department of Digital Innovation and Technology Department of Food and Health Sciences Department of Hospitality and Business Management Department of Sport and Recreation School of General Education and Languages Current Student Admission Research THEi Research Centre Applied Impact Research Students Applied Research Presentations Research Repository Collaboration Work-Study Degree Programmes Work-Study Degree Scheme for BSE On-the-job-training Allowance Pilot Scheme Work-integrated Learning THEi – Lions Clubs Innov8 Enterprise Start-up Centre Employ our students News & Media Rooms Visitors Getting To THEi Visiting THEi Local School or Academic Organisation General Public or Other Organisations Facilities THEi Souvenirs Dining Society Smoke-Free Campus Contact Us Publication ✕ Post Specification TITLE : Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (Master of Science in Urban Forestry) Department of Construction, Environment and Engineering Ref No.: DCEE/PROFESSORIAL(MScUF)/09/26 Major Duties: The appointee shall report to the Programme Leader and the Head of Department and engage in teaching and learning activities, develop programme curriculum and teaching, learning and assessment materials, support students in their learning, participate in academic and scholarly activities of the Department, and undertake academic and administrative support services for the Master of Science in Urban Forestry (MScUF) programme. The appointee is expected to contribute to the planning, development, implementation, and periodic review of the MScUF programme.  The appointee will take part in teaching and supervising capstone applied projects and student work, delivering a high-quality programme, and leading and participating in scholarly activities, including but not limited to research, consultancy, networking, and collaboration with industry partners to promote the Institute and the programme.  S/He will also be expected to maintain close contact with industry, commerce, and other educational institutions on collaborative arrangements to promote and ensure the relevance and excellence of the programme. The appointee will also assist in the formulation of learning and teaching strategies and curriculum development in at least one of the following modules: Capstone Applied Project Culture Conservation & Management in Urban Forestry Entrepreneurial Leadership in Urban Forestry Geographical Information System & Tree Inventory Management Innovative Technologies & Applications in Urban Forestry Plant Culture Recreational Management & Planning in Urban Forests Sustainable Urban Forestry & Arboriculture Traditional Chinese Yuanlin Theory & Practice Urban Ecosystem Ecology Urban Forest Ecophysiology Urban Forestry Policy & Governance Urban Planning & Green Infrastructure Requirements: The successful candidate should have a recognised Doctoral degree in Horticulture, Geography, Environmental Science, Botany, Ecology, Landscape Management, Urban Planning or a related discipline, together with solid teaching experience at the tertiary level.  The candidate should also have good professional standing with strong industry networks and achievements in professional practice and applied research activities.  The candidate should possess a strong track record of research publications.  A proven record of collaboration with industry or professional bodies would be an advantage. S/He should have good interpersonal and communication skills, and a high level of proficiency in written and spoken English and Chinese, including Putonghua.  S/He must also fulfil one of the following criteria: (a) Mother tongue/language is Putonghua; or (b) Received a recognised Bachelor’s degree or above for which the Medium of Instruction (MOI) was Putonghua; or (c) At least 3 years’ work experience in Chinese Mainland or other Putonghua-speaking countries or regions; or (d) Attained one of the following qualifications: (i) Grade B, Level 2 or above in the Putonghua Shuiping Ceshi (PSC) – Putonghua Proficiency Test administered by the State Language Commission; or (ii) Level 3 or above in the Language Proficiency Assessment for Teachers (Putonghua) administered by the Hong Kong Examinations and Assessment Authority (HKEEA) or equivalent. Notes: (1) The Medium of Instruction of the MScUF programme is Putonghua. (2) The appointee may be required to perform duties at different locations and work irregular hours, shifts, and weekends, as necessary. (3) The remuneration package will be competitive and commensurate with the appointee’s qualifications and experience. (4) The appointee will work at the Chai Wan Campus and/or nearby teaching premises. Application Procedures: A completed application form [THEi-HR-601 (Dec 2025)] , together with a full curriculum vitae (CV) , should be sent to thei-jobs@thei.edu.hk . Applicants should take note of the following: (1) The completed application form and a detailed CV should be combined into one PDF file with a file size below 10MB . (2) The file should be saved with the applicant’s name as “surname and given name”, e.g. “CHAN Siu-lam.pdf”. (3) For the email subject, please cite “Application for Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (MScUF) (Ref No.: DCEE/PROFESSORIAL(MScUF)/09/26)” and state the specialised stream on the application form. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until the post is filled. The Institute reserves the right not to fill the post. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. Information on unsuccessful candidates will normally be destroyed 12 months after completion of the recruitment exercise. Download Application Form in PDF format 3890 8000 3890 8339 info@thei.edu.hk 133 Shing Tai Road,  Chai Wan, Hong Kong Rm C215a, 2/F, Blk C, IVE(TY), 20 Tsing Yi Rd, Tsing Yi Island, NT Connect with THEi Resources For Current Students For Staff For Alumni For Visitors Copyright © 2026. Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong. All rights reserved. Privacy Disclaimer 3890 8000 3890 8339 info@thei.edu.hk 133 Shing Tai Road,  Chai Wan, Hong Kong Rm C215a, 2/F, Blk C, IVE(TY), 20 Tsing Yi Rd, Tsing Yi Island, NT Connect with THEi Resources For Current Students For Staff For Alumni For Visitors Copyright © 2026. Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong. All rights reserved. Privacy Disclaimer Login with your site account Lost your password? Remember Me"
    },
