      "title": "Senior Lecturer (Master of Science in Urban Forestry)",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer (Master of Science in Urban Forestry) - Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong Back About Vision and Mission Senior Management Strategic Plan Governance & Organisation Departments Department of Construction, Environment and Engineering Department of Design and Architecture Department of Digital Innovation and Technology Department of Food and Health Sciences Department of Hospitality and Business Management Department of Sport and Recreation School of General Education and Languages Current Student Admission Research THEi Research Centre Applied Impact Research Students Applied Research Presentations Research Repository Collaboration Work-Study Degree Programmes Work-Study Degree Scheme for BSE On-the-job-training Allowance Pilot Scheme Work-integrated Learning THEi – Lions Clubs Innov8 Enterprise Start-up Centre Employ our students News & Media Rooms Visitors Getting To THEi Visiting THEi Local School or Academic Organisation General Public or Other Organisations Facilities THEi Souvenirs Dining Society Smoke-Free Campus Contact Us Publication Staff Jobs EN 繁 简 Staff Jobs EN 繁 简 About Vision and Mission Senior Management Strategic Plan Governance & Organisation Departments Department of Construction, Environment and Engineering Department of Design and Architecture Department of Digital Innovation and Technology Department of Food and Health Sciences Department of Hospitality and Business Management Department of Sport and Recreation School of General Education and Languages Current Student Admission Research THEi Research Centre Applied Impact Research Students Applied Research Presentations Research Repository Collaboration Work-Study Degree Programmes Work-Study Degree Scheme for BSE On-the-job-training Allowance Pilot Scheme Work-integrated Learning THEi – Lions Clubs Innov8 Enterprise Start-up Centre Employ our students News & Media Rooms Visitors Getting To THEi Visiting THEi Local School or Academic Organisation General Public or Other Organisations Facilities THEi Souvenirs Dining Society Smoke-Free Campus Contact Us Publication ✕ Post Specification TITLE : Senior Lecturer (Master of Science in Urban Forestry) Department of Construction, Environment and Engineering Ref No.: DCEE/SL(MScUF)/09/26 Major Duties: The appointee shall report to the Programme Leader and the Head of Department and engage in teaching and learning activities, develop programme curriculum and teaching, learning and assessment materials, support students in their learning, participate in academic and scholarly activities of the Department, and undertake academic and administrative support services for the Master of Science in Urban Forestry (MScUF) programmee. The appointee will also assist in the formulation of learning and teaching strategies and curriculum development in at least one of the following modules: Capstone Applied Project Culture Conservation & Management in Urban Forestry Entrepreneurial Leadership in Urban Forestry Geographical Information System & Tree Inventory Management Innovative Technologies & Applications in Urban Forestry Plant Culture Recreational Management & Planning in Urban Forests Sustainable Urban Forestry & Arboriculture Traditional Chinese Yuanlin Theory & Practice Urban Ecosystem Ecology Urban Forest Ecophysiology Urban Forestry Policy & Governance Urban Planning & Green Infrastructure Requirements: The successful candidate should have a recognised Doctoral degree in Horticulture, Geography, Environmental Science, Botany, Ecology, Landscape Management, Urban Planning or a related discipline, together with solid teaching experience at the tertiary level and/or experience in professional practice in the related fields. S/He should have experience in supervising students’ Final Year Projects, and have good interpersonal and communication skills, and a high level of proficiency in written and spoken English and Chinese, including Putonghua.  A proven record of collaboration with industry or professional bodies would be an advantage.  S/He must also fulfil one of the following criteria: (a) Mother tongue/language is Putonghua; or (b) Received a recognised Bachelor’s degree or above of which the Medium of Instruction (MOI) was Putonghua; or (c) Has at least over 3 years’ work experience in Chinese Mainland or other Putonghua-speaking countries or regions; or (d) Achieved at least Grade B, Level 2 in the Putonghua Shuiping Ceshi (PSC) – Putonghua Proficiency Test administered by the State Language Commission. Notes: (1) The Medium of Instruction of the MScUF programme is Putonghua. (2) The post is at the rank of “Teaching Fellow I”. (3) The appointee may be required to perform duties at different locations and work irregular hours, shifts, and weekends as necessary. (4) The remuneration package will be competitive and commensurate with the appointee’s qualifications and experience. (5) The appointee will work at the Chai Wan Campus and/or nearby teaching premises. Application Procedures: A completed application form [THEi-HR-601 (Dec 2025)] , together with a full curriculum vitae (CV) , should be sent to thei-jobs@thei.edu.hk . Applicants should take note of the following: (1) The completed application form and detailed CV should be combined into one PDF file with a file size below 10MB . (2) The file should be saved with the applicant’s name as “surname and given name”, e.g. “CHAN Siu-lam.pdf”. (3) For the email subject, please cite “Application for Senior Lecturer (MScUF), DCEE (Ref No.: DCEE/SL(MScUF)/09/26)”. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until the post is filled. The Institute reserves the right not to fill the post. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. Information on unsuccessful candidates will normally be destroyed 12 months after completion of the recruitment exercise. Download Application Form in PDF format 3890 8000 3890 8339 info@thei.edu.hk 133 Shing Tai Road,  Chai Wan, Hong Kong Rm C215a, 2/F, Blk C, IVE(TY), 20 Tsing Yi Rd, Tsing Yi Island, NT Connect with THEi Resources For Current Students For Staff For Alumni For Visitors Copyright © 2026. Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong. All rights reserved. Privacy Disclaimer 3890 8000 3890 8339 info@thei.edu.hk 133 Shing Tai Road,  Chai Wan, Hong Kong Rm C215a, 2/F, Blk C, IVE(TY), 20 Tsing Yi Rd, Tsing Yi Island, NT Connect with THEi Resources For Current Students For Staff For Alumni For Visitors Copyright © 2026. Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong. All rights reserved. Privacy Disclaimer Login with your site account Lost your password? Remember Me"
