    "https://thei.edu.hk/human-resources-officer-ref-o-thei-hro-hro-06-26/": {
      "title": "Human Resources Officer",
      "description": "Human Resources Officer - Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong Back About Vision and Mission Senior Management Strategic Plan Governance & Organisation Departments Department of Construction, Environment and Engineering Department of Design and Architecture Department of Digital Innovation and Technology Department of Food and Health Sciences Department of Hospitality and Business Management Department of Sport and Recreation School of General Education and Languages Current Student Admission Research THEi Research Centre Applied Impact Research Students Applied Research Presentations Research Repository Collaboration Work-Study Degree Programmes Work-Study Degree Scheme for BSE On-the-job-training Allowance Pilot Scheme Work-integrated Learning THEi – Lions Clubs Innov8 Enterprise Start-up Centre Employ our students News & Media Rooms Visitors Getting To THEi Visiting THEi Local School or Academic Organisation General Public or Other Organisations Facilities THEi Souvenirs Dining Society Smoke-Free Campus Contact Us Publication Staff Jobs EN 繁 简 Staff Jobs EN 繁 简 About Vision and Mission Senior Management Strategic Plan Governance & Organisation Departments Department of Construction, Environment and Engineering Department of Design and Architecture Department of Digital Innovation and Technology Department of Food and Health Sciences Department of Hospitality and Business Management Department of Sport and Recreation School of General Education and Languages Current Student Admission Research THEi Research Centre Applied Impact Research Students Applied Research Presentations Research Repository Collaboration Work-Study Degree Programmes Work-Study Degree Scheme for BSE On-the-job-training Allowance Pilot Scheme Work-integrated Learning THEi – Lions Clubs Innov8 Enterprise Start-up Centre Employ our students News & Media Rooms Visitors Getting To THEi Visiting THEi Local School or Academic Organisation General Public or Other Organisations Facilities THEi Souvenirs Dining Society Smoke-Free Campus Contact Us Publication ✕ Post Specification TITLE : Human Resources Officer Human Resources Office Ref No.: HRO/HRO/06/26 Major Duties: (a) To perform administrative duties in the following human resources and central services: staff recruitment and appointment, compensation and benefits, training and development, staff relations and engagement, human resources management information system, and office administration; (b) To supervise and co-ordinate the work of supporting staff and ensure the effective delivery of services; (c) To assist in the formulation, implementation and review of operational policies, systems and procedures; (d) To undertake committee work in various boards and meetings; and (e) To provide executive and secretarial support to projects, functions and events. Requirements: (a) A recognised degree or equivalent; (b) At least two years’ relevant work experience at the executive level, preferably in Human Resources and/or in educational institutions or major organisations; (c) Good communication, inter-personal, organisational and administrative skills; (d) A pro-active approach and ability to work independently; and (e) Good command of spoken and written English and Chinese, preferably including Putonghua. Notes: (1) Applicants who have responded to the advertisement in the last six months need not re-apply. (2) The post is at the rank of “Officer”. (3) Shortlisted applicants will be required to attend and pass a written test. (4) The appointee may be required to perform duties at different locations, and to work irregular hours, shifts and weekends, as necessary. (5) The remuneration package will be competitive and commensurate with the appointee’s qualifications and experience. (6) The appointee will work at the Chai Wan Campus. Application Procedures: A completed application form [THEi-HR-601 (Dec 2025)] , together with a full curriculum vitae (CV) , should be sent to thei-jobs@thei.edu.hk . Applicants should take note of the following: (1) Completed application form and detailed CV should be combined into one PDF file with a file size below 10MB . (2) The file should be saved with the applicant’s name as “surname and given name”, e.g. “CHAN Siu-lam.pdf”. (3) For the email subject, please cite “Application for Human Resources Officer, HRO (Ref No.: HRO/HRO/06/26)”. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until the post is filled. The Institute reserves the right not to fill the post. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. Information on unsuccessful candidates will normally be destroyed 12 months after completion of the recruitment exercise. Download Application Form in PDF format 3890 8000 3890 8339 info@thei.edu.hk 133 Shing Tai Road,  Chai Wan, Hong Kong Rm C215a, 2/F, Blk C, IVE(TY), 20 Tsing Yi Rd, Tsing Yi Island, NT Connect with THEi Resources For Current Students For Staff For Alumni For Visitors Copyright © 2026. Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong. All rights reserved. Privacy Disclaimer 3890 8000 3890 8339 info@thei.edu.hk 133 Shing Tai Road,  Chai Wan, Hong Kong Rm C215a, 2/F, Blk C, IVE(TY), 20 Tsing Yi Rd, Tsing Yi Island, NT Connect with THEi Resources For Current Students For Staff For Alumni For Visitors Copyright © 2026. Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong. All rights reserved. Privacy Disclaimer Login with your site account Lost your password? Remember Me"
    },
    "https://thei.edu.hk/officer-ref-o-thei-po-off-01-26/": {
      "title": "Officer",
      "description": "Officer - Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong Back About Vision and Mission Senior Management Strategic Plan Governance & Organisation Departments Department of Construction, Environment and Engineering Department of Design and Architecture Department of Digital Innovation and Technology Department of Food and Health Sciences Department of Hospitality and Business Management Department of Sport and Recreation School of General Education and Languages Current Student Admission Research THEi Research Centre Applied Impact Research Students Applied Research Presentations Research Repository Collaboration Work-Study Degree Programmes Work-Study Degree Scheme for BSE On-the-job-training Allowance Pilot Scheme Work-integrated Learning THEi – Lions Clubs Innov8 Enterprise Start-up Centre Employ our students News & Media Rooms Visitors Getting To THEi Visiting THEi Local School or Academic Organisation General Public or Other Organisations Facilities THEi Souvenirs Dining Society Smoke-Free Campus Contact Us Publication Staff Jobs EN 繁 简 Staff Jobs EN 繁 简 About Vision and Mission Senior Management Strategic Plan Governance & Organisation Departments Department of Construction, Environment and Engineering Department of Design and Architecture Department of Digital Innovation and Technology Department of Food and Health Sciences Department of Hospitality and Business Management Department of Sport and Recreation School of General Education and Languages Current Student Admission Research THEi Research Centre Applied Impact Research Students Applied Research Presentations Research Repository Collaboration Work-Study Degree Programmes Work-Study Degree Scheme for BSE On-the-job-training Allowance Pilot Scheme Work-integrated Learning THEi – Lions Clubs Innov8 Enterprise Start-up Centre Employ our students News & Media Rooms Visitors Getting To THEi Visiting THEi Local School or Academic Organisation General Public or Other Organisations Facilities THEi Souvenirs Dining Society Smoke-Free Campus Contact Us Publication ✕ Post Specification TITLE : Officer President’s Office Ref No.: PO/OFF/01/26 Major Duties: (a) To assist in the preparation and compilation of management reports, progress update reports, statistics, proposals, returns of information, presentation slides and other meeting materials, reports or documentations for various meetings, events and purposes; (b) To organise, manage and provide secretarial support to various meetings, committees and boards, including the preparation of minutes and agendas; (c) To organise, coordinate and support various events, functions and forums, either for the President’s Office or for the Institute; (d) To prepare official correspondence including emails and letters; (e) To liaise with internal and external parties on behalf of the President’s Office; (f) To provide administrative support to the operation of the President’s Office; (g) To coordinate or assist in the arrangement of visits for external guests; and (h) To handle ad hoc projects and assignments as required to support operational needs of the President’s Office or the Institute. Requirements: (a) A recognised degree or equivalent qualification; (b) At least 2 years’ relevant work experience at executive level, preferably in educational institutions or comparable organisations; (c) Detail-oriented, organised, proactive, with strong sense of responsibility, time management skill and the ability to multi-task independently as well as be a good team player; (d) Good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese, with strong interpersonal and communication skills; (e) Priority will be given to applicants who have solid experience in report, meeting minutes and/or proposal writing in previous work; (f) Able to appropriately handle confidential information and materials; and (g) High proficiency in computer software applications, including MS Word, MS Excel, MS PowerPoint, and Chinese word processing. Notes: (1) Applicants who have responded to the advertisement in the last six months need not re-apply. (2) Shortlisted applicants will be required to attend and pass a written test. (3) The appointee may be required to perform duties at different sites and outside Hong Kong, and work irregular hours, shifts and on Saturdays and Sundays as necessary. (4) The remuneration package will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. (5) The appointee will work at the Chai Wan Campus. Application Procedures: A completed application form [THEi-HR-601 (Dec 2025)] , together with a full curriculum vitae , should be sent to thei-jobs@thei.edu.hk . Applicants should take note of the following: (1) Completed application form and detailed curriculum vitae (CV) should be combined into one file in PDF format with a file size below 10MB . (2) The file should be saved with the applicant’s name as “surname and given name”, e.g. “CHAN Siu-lam.pdf”. (3) For the email subject, please cite “Application for Officer, PO (Ref No.: PO/OFF/01/26)”. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until the post is filled. The Institute reserves the right not to fill the post. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. Information on unsuccessful candidates will normally be destroyed 12 months after completion of the recruitment exercise. Download Application Form in PDF format 3890 8000 3890 8339 info@thei.edu.hk 133 Shing Tai Road,  Chai Wan, Hong Kong Rm C215a, 2/F, Blk C, IVE(TY), 20 Tsing Yi Rd, Tsing Yi Island, NT Connect with THEi Resources For Current Students For Staff For Alumni For Visitors Copyright © 2026. Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong. All rights reserved. Privacy Disclaimer 3890 8000 3890 8339 info@thei.edu.hk 133 Shing Tai Road,  Chai Wan, Hong Kong Rm C215a, 2/F, Blk C, IVE(TY), 20 Tsing Yi Rd, Tsing Yi Island, NT Connect with THEi Resources For Current Students For Staff For Alumni For Visitors Copyright © 2026. Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong. All rights reserved. Privacy Disclaimer Login with your site account Lost your password? Remember Me"
    },
    "https://thei.edu.hk/part-time-lecturer-aircraft-engineering-ref-no-dcee-ptl-ae-09-26/": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer (Aircraft Engineering)",
      "description": "Part-time Lecturer (Aircraft Engineering) - Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong Back About Vision and Mission Senior Management Strategic Plan Governance & Organisation Departments Department of Construction, Environment and Engineering Department of Design and Architecture Department of Digital Innovation and Technology Department of Food and Health Sciences Department of Hospitality and Business Management Department of Sport and Recreation School of General Education and Languages Current Student Admission Research THEi Research Centre Applied Impact Research Students Applied Research Presentations Research Repository Collaboration Work-Study Degree Programmes Work-Study Degree Scheme for BSE On-the-job-training Allowance Pilot Scheme Work-integrated Learning THEi – Lions Clubs Innov8 Enterprise Start-up Centre Employ our students News & Media Rooms Visitors Getting To THEi Visiting THEi Local School or Academic Organisation General Public or Other Organisations Facilities THEi Souvenirs Dining Society Smoke-Free Campus Contact Us Publication Staff Jobs EN 繁 简 Staff Jobs EN 繁 简 About Vision and Mission Senior Management Strategic Plan Governance & Organisation Departments Department of Construction, Environment and Engineering Department of Design and Architecture Department of Digital Innovation and Technology Department of Food and Health Sciences Department of Hospitality and Business Management Department of Sport and Recreation School of General Education and Languages Current Student Admission Research THEi Research Centre Applied Impact Research Students Applied Research Presentations Research Repository Collaboration Work-Study Degree Programmes Work-Study Degree Scheme for BSE On-the-job-training Allowance Pilot Scheme Work-integrated Learning THEi – Lions Clubs Innov8 Enterprise Start-up Centre Employ our students News & Media Rooms Visitors Getting To THEi Visiting THEi Local School or Academic Organisation General Public or Other Organisations Facilities THEi Souvenirs Dining Society Smoke-Free Campus Contact Us Publication ✕ Post Specification TITLE : Part-time Lecturer (Aircraft Engineering) Department of Construction, Environment and Engineering Ref No.: DCEE/PTL(AE)/09/26 Major Duties: The appointee shall engage in the delivery of lectures, tutorials, experiments, practical workshops and supervising student work for the Department.  The appointee shall also support students in their learning, participate in academic and scholarly activities of the Department, and provide academic and administrative support to sustain the daily operation of the programme and the HKAR-147 training organisation. Requirements: The successful candidate should have a recognised Master’s degree, preferably a Doctoral degree, in Aircraft Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace/Aeronautical Engineering, Electronics/Electrical Engineering, Applied Physics, Applied Mathematics, Statistics, or related fields, with at least 4 years of relevant teaching experience at the tertiary level and/or experience in professional practice in the relevant aviation fields. He/she should have good interpersonal and communication skills, a high level of proficiency in English and preferably Chinese (including Putonghua).  A proven record of linkage with industry or professional bodies will be an advantage. Preference will be given to candidates with advanced knowledge or work experience in aviation reliability engineering, propeller design and maintenance, aircraft system design and maintenance, aircraft powerplant systems, aircraft structural maintenance, composite repair, aircraft maintenance practices, aircraft electrical theories, aerodynamics (fluid and gas dynamics), aircraft certification (HKAR-21) and/or HKAR-145 and HKAR-147 operations.  Candidates with membership in professional institutions such as the Hong Kong Institution of Engineers and/or experience in conducting HKAR-66 licence training and/or holding a HKAR-66 licence, and/or being an HKAR-147 approved practical or knowledge instructor will also have an advantage. Notes: (1) The appointee may be required to perform duties at different locations and work irregular hours, including weekends, as necessary. (2) The remuneration package will be competitive and commensurate with the appointee’s qualifications and experience. (3) The appointee will mainly work at the Tsing Yi Campus. Application Procedures: A completed application form [THEi-HR-601 (Dec 2025)] , together with a full curriculum vitae (CV) , should be sent to thei-jobs@thei.edu.hk . Applicants should take note of the following: (1) The completed application form and a detailed CV should be combined into one PDF file with a file size below 10MB . (2) The file should be saved with the applicant’s name as “surname and given name”, e.g. “CHAN Siu-lam.pdf”. (3) For the email subject, please cite “Application for Part-time Lecturer (Aircraft Engineering), DCEE (Ref No.: DCEE/PTL(AE)/09/26)”. Closing date for applications: 29 October 2026 The Institute reserves the right not to fill the post.  Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only.  Information on unsuccessful candidates will normally be destroyed 12 months after completion of the recruitment exercise. Download Application Form in PDF format 3890 8000 3890 8339 info@thei.edu.hk 133 Shing Tai Road,  Chai Wan, Hong Kong Rm C215a, 2/F, Blk C, IVE(TY), 20 Tsing Yi Rd, Tsing Yi Island, NT Connect with THEi Resources For Current Students For Staff For Alumni For Visitors Copyright © 2026. Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong. All rights reserved. Privacy Disclaimer 3890 8000 3890 8339 info@thei.edu.hk 133 Shing Tai Road,  Chai Wan, Hong Kong Rm C215a, 2/F, Blk C, IVE(TY), 20 Tsing Yi Rd, Tsing Yi Island, NT Connect with THEi Resources For Current Students For Staff For Alumni For Visitors Copyright © 2026. Technological and Higher Education Institute of Hong Kong. All rights reserved. Privacy Disclaimer Login with your site account Lost your password? Remember Me"
